{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>אתם</b> Four verse-beginnings. Here. And the others: אתם לכו קחו לכם תבן — because Egypt did not want to give them straw; אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים; אתם נצבים; אתם עדי. To say: because אתם נצבים היום, you can forever be עדי, for I stand forever." "<b>ואביא אתכם אלי</b> Just as a woman is acquired by money, by document, and by bi'ah, so too Israel. By money — this is the plunder of Egypt. By document — this is the Torah, as stated: תורה צוה לנו משה מורשה — do not read מורשה (inheritance) but מאורשה (betrothed). By bi'ah — this is what is stated: ואפרוש כנפי עליך וגו' ואבא בברית אתך. Therefore Hosea said (Hosea 3:2) וארשתיך לי. ואביא = בביאה in gematria."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The four citations are verse-incipits beginning with the word אתם; only the first carries the lemma's own verse context. The last two are unaddressed in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:38.091850823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}